WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:05.910
The Highlander franchise is a series of stories
based around one compelling, original idea:

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.809
a fight between the world's Immortals, who
have secretly walked among us since the dawn

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.809
of time.

00:00:10.809 --> 00:00:14.990
The original movie revolves around Immortal
Connor MacLeod, from his youth in the fields

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:19.970
of medieval Scotland to 1980s New York City,
where the last Immortals are being drawn by

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.340
destiny to fight each other to the death.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:27.160
As we work our way up to the remake set to
be helmed by John Wick co-director Chad Stahelski,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.720
we're catching up with the untold truth of
Highlander.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.340
It came from the bathroom

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:38.489
"From the dawn of time we came, moving silently
down through the centuries…"

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:43.690
Spoken sonorously by Sean Connery, who played
the Immortal Ramirez, the film's brief introductory

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.100
monologue tells you everything you need to
know.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.921
As it turns out, Connery recorded the iconic
intro to the series in his bathroom, which

00:00:50.921 --> 00:00:52.300
is why it echoes so much.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.430
So the next time you hear that powerful intro,
just know that it's Sean Connery standing

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:01.420
half-naked in his vacation home, holding the
script in one hand, the phone in the other,

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.380
trying not to bump his knee on the toilet.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.520
That's great acting, people.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.440
"How revolting!

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:08.740
Achoo!"

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.650
There are still unreleased Queen songs

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.110
"Here we are!

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.380
Born to be kings!"

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:21.070
The value of Queen in the original Highlander
can simply not be overstated.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:23.970
It's impossible to imagine the movie without
the band's music.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.320
But despite how heavily Queen's music features
in the franchise, there was never an official

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.320
soundtrack.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:34.610
Instead, many songs from the movie ended up
on unofficial releases and Queen's 12th studio

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:37.290
album, 1986's A Kind of Magic.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.620
While the big numbers are all there, there
are Queen songs in the movie that have yet

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:42.610
to make it onto any album.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.720
The most notable omission being the band's
cover of "Theme from New York, New York" as

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.979
it plays in the lead-up to the climactic final
battle.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.000
"If I can make it there…

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.720
I'll make it anywhere!"

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.840
To date, only about 40 seconds of the song
has been released.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:05.370
Allegedly, Freddie Mercury hated singing it,
which is why it's never been released.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.440
And also, it sounds more than a little ridiculous.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.290
Christopher Lambert's peculiar accent

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:15.470
One of the most enigmatic and charming things
about the original Highlander is Christopher

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:19.779
Lambert's legendarily weird accent, which,
just like the actor, is impossible to pin

00:02:19.779 --> 00:02:20.779
down.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.700
"Christopher motherf---ing Lambert.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:24.739
The lord of the apes!

00:02:24.739 --> 00:02:25.739
Lord Raiden!

00:02:25.739 --> 00:02:26.819
And once lord of Diane Lane.

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:29.519
The guy had sex with Diane Lane!

00:02:29.519 --> 00:02:30.519
Multiple times!"

00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:35.459
The movie even references his unusual accent,
intentionally or not, when a police officer

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:39.639
notices MacLeod's inflection and pointedly
asks him where he comes from, netting the

00:02:39.639 --> 00:02:40.700
cheeky reply,

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.309
"You talk funny, Nash.

00:02:42.309 --> 00:02:43.309
Where you from?"

00:02:43.309 --> 00:02:44.950
"Lots of different places."

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.760
This was less of an intentional acting choice
than simply a happy accident.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:53.299
Reportedly, the accent came as a result of
Lambert's limited grasp of English at the

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:54.450
time of filming.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.650
Though born in New York, he was raised and
started his acting career in France.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:03.760
At the time of Highlander's filming, his only
prior English-speaking role had been an inarticulate

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.709
Tarzan who's only just learning English.

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:10.620
Not really an excuse for a guy who's been
around for hundreds of years, because it doesn't

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.900
get much weirder than this.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.020
"You have better things to do than lie there
on your ass."

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.120
The blind Highlander

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:24.469
Christopher Lambert must have been completely
lost during the filming of these movies.

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:28.730
In addition to being very iffy with English,
Lambert couldn't actually see much of what

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.319
he was doing either.

00:03:30.319 --> 00:03:35.510
Lambert suffers from myopia, a disorder that
blurs his vision, and filmed all of his work

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.359
without his much-needed glasses.

00:03:37.359 --> 00:03:41.719
It's one thing to just talk with your eyes
closed; it's a very different, way-more-dangerous

00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:43.959
thing to conduct hand-to-hand combat.

00:03:43.959 --> 00:03:48.280
In addition to nearly taking a tooth out of
co-star Michael Ironside's head during filming

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:52.040
of the sequel, Lambert got his own finger
split open because he couldn't see a swing

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.040
coming.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.989
It's kind of remarkable that it took a whole
movie and a half before Lambert was injured.

00:03:56.989 --> 00:04:01.049
Couldn't they just let the Immortal wear glasses?

00:04:01.049 --> 00:04:02.529
There's a recut sequel

00:04:02.529 --> 00:04:06.939
What is there to say about Highlander II:
The Quickening that hasn't already been spat

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:07.969
by Roger Ebert?

00:04:07.969 --> 00:04:12.169
"By the way, all of this insanity could have
added up to something that would have made

00:04:12.169 --> 00:04:13.529
a great, bad movie!

00:04:13.529 --> 00:04:17.570
But Highlander 2 is so crazily put together,
you get the impression that a lot of the key

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.630
scenes were just never filmed."

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:24.600
A movie so bad it has to be seen to be believed,
the puzzling follow-up received generally

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.250
terrible reviews.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:31.880
No longer coming "from the dawn of time" as
ageless enigmas, Highlander II "reveals" the

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:36.400
earthbound Immortals to actually be...aliens!

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:37.880
From the planet...Zeist!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:42.590
And sets the action on an Earth artificially
darkened by a man-made solar shield.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:47.470
Which is a plot goofy and cartoonishly evil
enough to be used by The Simpsons a few years

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.160
later.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:55.430
Because it was so bizarre, Highlander II was
essentially ignored in continuity.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.840
But there was another, later cut that aimed
to improve the sequel's quality.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:03.460
Marketed as the "Renegade Version," the newer
cut makes the movie better simply by cutting

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:07.430
out a lot of the weirder elements that made
the theatrical release so awful.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:11.880
It's still not a great movie, but it's not
one of the worst ones of all time, either.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.150
Weird cameos

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:16.690
It's possible that you might know Highlander
better from the long-running TV show, rather

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:18.340
than the movie that spawned it.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:22.020
"In the end, there can be only one.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.320
May it be Duncan McLeod."

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:28.280
Starring Adrian Paul, the series ran for six
seasons throughout the mid-90s, a precursor

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:33.400
to other relatively cheesy fantasy series
of the time like Xena: Warrior Princess or

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.240
Hercules: The Legendary Journeys.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:39.900
The series exists mostly as a cultural artifact,
featuting wild celebrity cameos from the likes

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:45.210
of rock star Joan Jett, porn star Traci Lords,
and Rowdy Roddy Piper, among others.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:48.200
It's one of the main reasons to watch the
series today.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.840
Because it's one thing to see a guest star
recite lines on Law &amp; Order — but it's a

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:57.720
completely different thing to see, say, Scottish
singer-songwriter Sheena Easton swinging a

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:58.720
sword around.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:01.470
"Damn you, Duncan McLeod."

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:03.640
There was another TV show

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:08.630
Barely remembered now, 1998 saw the release
of a short-lived spinoff to the series called

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.720
The Raven.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:14.590
Starring former Miss America Elizabeth Gracen,
the series followed the Immortal thief Amanda

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:19.920
and her ex-cop buddy as they solved crimes,
and sought redemption for past sins.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:23.380
General franchise fatigue caused The Raven
to never really catch on.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:28.450
Rumors of production difficulties, and a reported
tryst with Gracen and former president Bill

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.300
Clinton years earlier, killed the series.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.040
The Raven ran for just one season...

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:35.310
"There can be only one!

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.310
Ungh!"

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:41.140
...ending the Highlander franchise's live-action
presence on TV after a seven-year run.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.630
There was an anime

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:47.920
There's a far fringe to the Highlander franchise
where the continuity starts to get even weirder:

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.200
like the Highlander anime movie, which actually
scored positive reviews.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:56.160
Called The Search for Vengeance, the film
was written by Highlander series alum David

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:00.800
Abramowitz, which gives it a level of fan
credibility that many of the live action sequels

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:01.870
can't even claim.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:06.550
It's also probably the only fringe media in
the Highlander universe that might be worth

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:07.550
your time.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:12.060
Meanwhile, Highlander: The Animated Series
is best left forgotten, as is the clunky game

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.300
based on the cartoon.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:20.880
The 1986 game wasn't much better, either.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.740
And in 2001, an online MMO was in development,
but eventually cancelled.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:28.700
Yet another game, developed nearly a decade
later for next-gen systems, was canceled in

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:32.470
development, leaving behind only a remarkably
unpromising trailer.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.880
The moral of the story: let's not dismiss
the remake, okay?

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:40.750
Could it be any weirder, worse, or off-base
than what's come before?

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:41.940
Probably not.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.030
Thanks for watching!

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:45.510
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:47.620
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

